\details{
The derivative is taken by central differences of the DESIGN, not of
the fitted values, so the estimate and its standard error describe one
function rather than two. Writing \code{D} for the differenced design and
\code{V} for the joint coefficient covariance, the reported curve is \verb{D c}
and its covariance is \verb{D V D'}, which is exact for the differenced
basis; the only approximation is the difference itself, and \code{eps}
